    "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
    "headline": "Special Weather Statement issued September 18 at 6:26PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
    "description": "At 626 PM MDT, Doppler radar was tracking a strong thunderstorm 19\nmiles southwest of Dexter, or 23 miles south of Roswell, moving\nnortheast at 20 mph.\n\nHAZARD...Wind gusts up to 50 mph and half inch size hail.\n\nSOURCE...Radar indicated.\n\nIMPACT...Gusty winds could knock down tree limbs and blow around\nunsecured objects. Minor damage to outdoor objects is\npossible.\n\nLocations impacted include...\nSouthern Roswell, Dexter, Roswell Correctional Facility and\nGreenfield.\n\nThis includes Highway 285 between Mile Markers 89 and 104.",
    "instruction": "Monitor the weather situation closely and be alert for threatening\nweather conditions.",
