    "event": "Flood Advisory",
    "sender": "w-nws.webmaster@noaa.gov",
    "senderName": "NWS Albuquerque NM",
    "headline": "Flood Advisory issued September 18 at 6:22PM MDT until September 18 at 8:15PM MDT by NWS Albuquerque NM",
    "description": "* WHAT...Arroyo and small stream flooding caused by excessive\nrainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Socorro County in central New Mexico...\nSouthern Cibola County in west central New Mexico...\n\n* WHEN...Until 815 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- At 620 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. This  will cause arroyo and small stream flooding.\nBetween 1 and 1.5 inches of rain have fallen.\n- Additional rainfall amounts of 0.5 to 1 inch are expected over\nthe area. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nAlamo.\n- Indian Route 169 north of Alamo, NM crossing the Waterbury Draw.\n- http://www.weather.gov/safety/flood",
    "instruction": "Turn around, don't drown when encountering flooded roads. Most flood\ndeaths occur in vehicles.",
    "response": "Avoid",
